    "description": "-Lead Developer for an underwriting registration redesign effort. The application included integration with Sybase databases and multiple back-end Notes databases. Developed the Domino Web Services proof of concept tool that was used for the basis of the future WebMethods to Domino Web Service. \n-Developer (Acting Lead) for effort to develop a Domino web-based application to manage 150,000 user IDs, 20,000 company accounts, and real-time password resets. The application included custom APIs to integrate Domino with Tivoli Access Manager, Web Methods, and PeopleSoft via Application Messaging (JAVA).\n-Lead developer for a web-based application to allow Multifamily customers to manage (add/modify/delete) their user IDs and reset user passwords.  The application managed 1,200+ users IDs. The application was developed using JAVA as the primary language for back-end agents, with the use of XML, XSL, HTML, DHTML, JavaScript to generate the user interface.\n-Lead developer for a Human Resource web-based recruitment application that is completely integrated into PeopleSoft’s HRMS module. The application handles the entire process, from creating a staffing requisition, initiating workflow and approvals, posting the jobs to an internal and external web sites, accepting resumes, and loading resumes into PeopleSoft’s HRMS module.  Integration with PeopleSoft and its Oracle back-end is accomplished through Lotus Connectors, Notrix, and PeopleSoft’s Application Messaging API.\n-Lead Developer for multiple Domino web and client based applications utilizing custom workflow (and Lotus WorkflowTM) and integration with (Oracle, Sybase, UDB) relational databases.",
