      "description": "Tech Lead/Solutions Architect (2015 to present)\n* Solutions and integration Architect responsible for solutioning new contract related features, interfaces, and patterns.\n* Performed Salesforce development tech lead responsibilities, integration, and development work. Development work included creation of custom lightning components, custom objects, Visual force pages/controllers, apex classes, page layouts, validation rules, workflows, reports, dashboards, Lightning App Builder, email to case, etc. \n\nTech Lead  (September 2005 to 2015)\n* Architected, designed, and developed Java based utilities, interfaces, and UI components running on the Domino platform, to automate the creation of Mortgage Backed Securities (MBS) contracts and related pricing components and integration. \n* Architected, designed, and built REST based web services to listen for service calls from new MBS commitment and pricing systems as well as outbound REST service calls.\n* Lead developer for the acquisitions contracting application suite that supported 750+ internal users. The contracting application is built on IBM Notes/Domino and manages lender data, legal language, pricing, Mortgage Backed Securities (MBS), and hundreds of other Mortgage related attributes.\n* Developed multiple Domino prototypes; Domino Pub/Sub model using a TIBCO ESB, configurable XML based loan pricing sheets transformed to HTML UI via XSLT, Domino based dynamic web service application, multiple Domino to COTs integrations\n* Designed, developed, and implemented a Domino application (JAVA backend) to replicate and translate hierarchical Domino data (parent/response documents) to an Oracle RDB\n* Designed, developed, and implemented a Domino data driven web service utility to expose application data from any Domino Database\n* Lead developer responsible for several Domino application integration projects. One which integrated a Domino application to a custom.Net Portal and third party product, Oracle Identity Manager (OIM)",
